      'Rule example: Collect and claim more half-suits than the opposing team. Each claimed half-suit scores 1 point.',
      "Turn-flow example: 1. **Asking**: On your turn, ask any one specific player from the OTHER team for a specific card. A question is valid ONLY if: (a) You ask for a specific card (by value and suit), (b) You have another card in that half-suit in your hand, (c) The player you ask holds at least one card, (d) You do NOT ask for a card that is in your own hand. 2. **Successful Ask**: If the asked player has the card, they pass it to you face-up, and you keep the turn, asking another question. 3. **Failed Ask**: If the asked player does NOT have the card, your turn ends and it becomes their turn to ask. 4. **No Teammate Asking**: You may NEVER ask a teammate for a card. All questions must be directed to the opposing team. 5. **Claiming**: If you believe your team holds all 6 cards of a half-suit, you may claim it on your turn by saying 'Claim' and naming exactly who has which cards. If correct, your team scores the half-suit. If you state the location of even one card wrongly, the half-suit is cancelled and neither team gets it.",
